[comment {-*- tcl -*- doctools manpage}]
[manpage_begin request n 1.0]
[keywords request http https TclOO]
[copyright {2026 generated documentation}]
[moddesc   {A TclOO wrapper around the standard http package}]
[titledesc {Object wrapper for HTTP/HTTPS requests}]
[category Utility]
[require Tcl 8.6]
[require request 1.0]
[description]
[para]
The [package request] package provides a TclOO object class named [emph request].
It is a lightweight wrapper around the standard [cmd ::http::geturl] and
[cmd ::http::posturl] commands with support for stored request state, optional
TLS registration, and simple response validation.

[section Synopsis]
[example {
package require request
request create client
client configure -method GET -url https://www.example.com
set body [client execute]
puts $body
}]

[section Description]
The [cmd request] class maintains request settings on the object. The stored
attributes may be updated with [cmd configure] and queried with [cmd cget].
The [cmd execute] method performs the request and enforces a successful HTTP
response status.

[para] The instance stores the following request attributes:
[list_begin definitions]
[def [const method]]
The HTTP method to use for the request, such as [const GET], [const POST],
[const PUT], or [const DELETE].
[def [const url]]
The request URL.
[def [const body]]
The request body passed to [cmd ::http::posturl] when using [const POST] or
other methods that accept a payload.
[def [const headers]]
A list of HTTP headers to pass to the underlying http command.
[def [const tls]]
An optional boolean passed to the constructor. When true, the package loads
TLS support and registers the [cmd ::tls::socket] implementation for [const https]
requests.
[def [const http-options]]
Additional supported [cmd ::http::geturl] options may be set through
[cmd configure] or passed directly to [cmd request], [cmd get], or [cmd post].
[list_end]

[para] The object also retains the last response state after any request:
[list_begin definitions]
[def [const lastBody]]
The raw response body.
[def [const lastCode]]
The HTTP status code.
[def [const lastStatus]]
The HTTP status text.
[def [const lastMeta]]
The response headers metadata returned by [cmd ::http::meta].
[def [const lastToken]]
The token returned by the http package request call.
[list_end]

[section Methods]
[list_begin definitions]
[call [emph request] [cmd configure] [opt keyvaluelist]]
[call [emph request] [cmd configure] [arg field] [arg value] [opt ...]]

Set one or more stored request attributes. If called without arguments, returns a
dictionary containing the current [arg method], [arg url], [arg body],
[arg headers], and any configured HTTP option values.

[para] The method accepts either a dictionary of options or a list of key/value
pairs. Leading hyphens are accepted on field names.

[call [emph request] [cmd cget] [arg attr]]
Return the value of the named attribute. Valid attributes include [const method],
[const url], [const body], [const headers], [const lastBody], [const lastCode],
[const lastStatus], [const lastMeta], [const lastToken], and any additional
supported [cmd ::http::geturl] option that was previously configured.
An unknown attribute raises an error.

[call [emph request] [cmd execute]]
Execute the stored request parameters. Throws an exception if the request fails or
if the HTTP status code is not in the 2xx range. On success, returns the response
body.

[call [emph request] [cmd request] [arg method] [arg url] [opt keyvaluelist]]

Perform a one-shot HTTP request without modifying the stored object state.
The [arg body] and [arg headers] may be provided through named options, and
additional supported [cmd ::http::geturl] options may also be passed.
Returns the response body on success.

[call [emph request] [cmd get] [arg url] [opt keyvaluelist]]

Convenience wrapper for a GET request.

[call [emph request] [cmd post] [arg url] [opt keyvaluelist]]

Convenience wrapper for a POST request.

[call [emph request] [cmd lastResponse]]
Return the last request response as a list with [const body], [const code],
[const status], [const headers], and [const token].
[list_end]

[section Examples]
[example {
package require request

request create client
client configure -method GET -url https://www.example.com
set body [client execute]
puts "Response length: [string length $body]"
}]

[example {
package require request
request create client -method POST -url https://api.example.com/submit \
    -body {name=alice&action=save} -headers {Content-Type application/x-www-form-urlencoded}
set body [client execute]
puts $body
}]

[example {
package require request
request create client
client configure {
    method POST
    url https://api.example.com/submit
    headers {Content-Type application/json}
    body {"name":"alice"}
}
try {
    set body [client execute]
    puts $body
} on error {type msg} {
    puts stderr "Request failed ($type): $msg"
}
}]

[manpage_end]